                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "When MangaGamer announced that they've licenced Sorcery Jokers I couldn't believe it. 3rdEye is my second favorite VN studio and I thought that their games are rather unknown to many. I've already finished this VN 2 years ago in Japanese and this review is a quick summary of positives/negatives based on my experience from Japanese version + translation/technical stuff I've noticed by launching this game to check translation quality.\n\n+Interesting world\n+Multi protagonist system which is a better form of dual protagonist system from Gensou no Idea, 3rdEye previous game\n+Good art & CGs\n+High quality of translation - MangaGamer actually subbed fragments which were not subbed in original Japanese version (like Ring voice messages, at least I don't remember them subbed)\n+High tension battle music\n+VN is mostly kinetic, but you can choose order of scenes/which character to follow first which may change your overall experience\n+Asahi\n+Pretty good seiyuu cast - Kawashima Rino/Aoba Ringo/Sawasa Sawa are well known in this industry\n+Fully translated glossary\n+Long, but interesting and action packed\n+Non-intrusive references to previous 3rdEye titles\n-FPS drops\n-Haruto can be a bit annoying in the first part of the game\n\nOverall I gave this VN 8.5/10 on VNDB, so this is also my final rating here. Might edit this review after I have more experience with English version. Sincere thanks to MangaGamer for licencing this hidden gem. If you ever decide to licence Gensou no Idea you have my money.\n",
